    "aliases": ["Toxigen Discriminative", "ToxiGen (discriminative)"],
    "description": "Machine-generated statements, toxic and benign, about 13 minority groups, for implicit hate speech. Used in two ways. Generative: the model continues prompts, and a toxicity classifier labels each output; the metric is the share of toxic outputs. Discriminative: the model labels human-annotated statements as toxic or benign; the metric is accuracy. Results from the two tasks are not comparable.",
    "summary": "Measures whether the model writes or detects hateful statements about minority groups, even when they use no obvious slurs.",
